Electromagnetic Fields and Energy — Haus and Melcher (@em-haus: 0, is #reference, #part-of @em-sources) { r_1VKHEEC14B3VDGBA13T6K4JQNV
H. A. Haus and James R. Melcher, Massachusetts Institute of Technology. [Complete online teaching book](https://web.mit.edu/6.013_book/www/) · [Book navigation](https://web.mit.edu/6.013_book/www/book.html).

Read the whole book during the sustained electromechanical and material studies. Its development of fields, charge transport, quasistatic approximations, forces, energy and distributed systems provides a complementary path to the wave-oriented treatments. Work derivations and physical examples rather than extracting design recipes without their conditions.

The MIT landing page carries a 1998 MIT copyright and reserves rights; other MIT teaching references identify permission to use the text. Free online reading does not make this a CC book. The landing page was checked on 29 October 2026; its older frame navigation may require an ordinary browser. No book, frames or examples are copied here.

